course: dictionary
lesson: 6530
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One small word can have several meanings, and «net» is a good example. Its main meaning is a material made of string, thread or wire with holes in between, such as a fishing net or a goal net.
explain: The sentence tells you which meaning is needed. «Herons stand very still at the edge of garden ponds to catch fish, so pond owners use nets» is about something you catch fish with, not a website.
explain: Ask what the word is doing in the sentence. In «The net weight is 400 grams», net means what is left once the packaging is taken away. Try each meaning in the sentence and keep the one that makes sense.
fact: Net can be a noun (a net, nets), a verb (to net, netting) or an adjective (net weight).
fact: «Net» can mean a material with holes, made of string or wire, or a thing made of it.
fact: «The Net» is short for the internet.
fact: In maths, a net is a flat shape that can be folded to make a 3D shape: a cube's net has 6 squares.
fact: Net weight on food packets means the weight of the food alone, without the packaging.
exercise: «Herons stand very still at the edge of garden ponds to catch fish, so pond owners use nets or give the fish places to hide.» In this sentence, what is a net? | A flat shape that folds into a 3D shape | *Something made of string or thread with holes, used for catching | A website on the internet | A kind of bird
exercise: In maths, a cube's net has 6 squares. What is a net in maths? | A box made of wood | A line that goes round a circle | A tall shape with a point at the top | *A flat shape that can be folded to make a 3D shape
exercise: «Net weight on food packets means the food alone.» What does net mean here? | Caught in a fish trap | Tied together with string | Very heavy | *What is left after the packaging is taken away
test: In «Ben tried to net the butterfly before it flew away», what does net mean? | To shop online | To score a goal | To fold into a box | *To catch in a net
test: Sam says, «I spent an hour on the Net looking for facts about whales.» What is the Net? | A fishing boat | A sports game | A kind of fish | *The internet
exam: «Humpback whales work together to blow a spiral net of bubbles that traps a shoal of fish.» What does net mean here? | A website full of whale facts | *A trap made of bubbles, spread out like a net | A flat maths shape that folds into a box | A fishing boat that sails at night
